          "sub_type": "code",
          "content": "```txt\nRecitation Problems\nFormalize each group of sentences (using the given function and predicate symbols), then prove the last from the others using resolution and paramodulation.\nJane's lover drives a red car.\nFred is the only person who drives a red car.\nTherefore, Fred is Jane's lover.\n(L(x) = the lover of x; D(x) = x drives a red car)\nMrs. Abbot only teaches good students.\nJohn and Mary have the same teacher.\nMrs. Abbot is Mary's teacher.\nTherefore, John is a good student.\n(T(x) = the teacher of x; G(x) = x is a good student)\nLecture 9 • 18\n```",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.118,
                0.478,
                0.676,
                0.502
              ],
              "content": "Please do these recitation problems before the next recitation."
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": []
        }
      ]
